    "# Theta_reg analysis, rare vs typical events: September runs without the near-copy statistics\n",
    "\n",
    "Copy of `turb_theta_reg_rare_typical_sep.ipynb` (zfloor, full set of statistics) for the runs launched on 2026-10-01 with\n",
    "the three near-copy pairs of statistics removed:\n",
    "\n",
    "- **`L_6_psi` removed entirely** (`L_6[7]`/`L_6[8]` and `L_6_psi[20]`/`L_6_psi[21]` were near copies of each other);\n",
    "- **one slot of `Scalar_morlet_gaussianK` dropped**, channel 8 region 3 (`--drop_stats Scalar_morlet_gaussianK:8:3`), the near copy of `Scalar_psi_gaussianK[77]`.\n",
    "\n",
    "Two arms, 5 seeds each (900-904), choose with `ARM` in the config cell: `reg1e-4` (array job 465148) and `reg1e-2` (array job 465149).\n",
    "\n",
    "What changes compared to the full-set notebook:\n",
    "- `terms` (read from `config.json`) has no `L_6_psi`, so every family after `L_6` sits at different columns. Nothing below uses hard-coded column numbers: all ranges come from `theta_column_map` on the loaded potentials.\n",
    "- The dropped slot is not re-applied by hand. The saved fitted state of `Scalar_morlet_gaussianK` already excludes it (`active_flat`), so loading it gives the reduced φ directly. The loader **checks** that the loaded `drop_slots` are the ones in `config.json`.\n",
    "- These runs were launched with `--skip_reg_solve` and no offline solve has been done yet, so `LAM = None`: everything uses the sampler's $\\theta_t$ at the last step (`THETA_SOURCE = 'theta_t'`), as in the July notebook.\n",
    "\n",
    "Two sources of spread are reported: **across seeds** (every seed sees the same data `x1`) and a **bootstrap over the rare signals** (which signals happen to be rare).\n",
    "\n",
    "**How to use.** Settings are in the **Knobs** cell. After changing a knob, re-run from the *Whole-dataset rare/typical split* cell down.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Contents.** θ per family · load θ + potentials · rare/typical split (+ examples of each) · per-family energy by category · log p rare vs typical · Florentin's plot · 1. per-family gap D · 2. threshold robustness · 3. continuous version · 4. compensation · 5. residual variance · 6. model samples\n"
