    "## Whole-dataset rare/typical split\n",
    "\n",
    "Method from `extract_samples.ipynb`: a signal is **rare** if its extremeness, $\\max_t |x(t+1)-x(t)|$ (max absolute lag-1 increment), exceeds the `PERCENTILE`-th percentile (Knobs cell) of that quantity over the dataset. It is applied to `x1`: the wavelet-decomposed **and normalized** signals that `phi_X` is computed on. So the labels line up with `phi_X`, and the cutoff is in the same units as the model samples (section 6).\n",
    "\n",
    "`normalize` (`codes/utils.py`) is **global**: one scalar mean and one scalar std for the whole tensor, not per sample. A positive rescaling preserves the ranking, so the split should match one on un-normalized `Data[:n1]`; only the cutoff value changes, by the factor `Data[:n1].std()`. The cell checks both."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 13,
   "id": "da246800",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Whole dataset (n1=8500) split on x1 at p95: typical 8075, rare 425 | cutoff = 0.3128 in x1 units\n",
      "Old split on Data[:n1]: rare 425, cutoff (p95) = 1.004 in Data units | overlap with new rare set: 425/425 | cutoff ratio old/new = 3.21 vs Data[:n1].std() = 3.21\n"
     ]
