    "\n",
    "**What it does.**\n",
    "1. Take `N_W` data signals and fresh noise and put the walkers **exactly on the interpolant** at a time $t_0$. Their moments are then exactly right at $t_0$.\n",
    "2. Make **one step** of the run's own code (`iteration_step_projection`: drift + noise $\\sqrt{2h}\\,\\sigma$, then the single linear corrector; same ridge, mask and float64 as the run) to $t_0+h$.\n",
