    "---\n",
    "# 🧪 TEST 2026-10-08 (C): do the 11 missed moments matter for the fine-scale wavelet marginals?\n",
    "\n",
    "**Separate testing experiment, not part of the rare/typical analysis.** Everything from here to \"END OF TEST 2026-10-08\" belongs to it. It only reads what the cells above built. Every new variable starts with `mg_`. θ is not used.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Why.** Test (A) showed that the 11 moments the run misses come from the single corrector per step. Before changing the code we want to know whether the miss is visible in the physics. The 11 moments are Scalar region statistics of the **finest wavelet channels, inner regions**: how many fine-scale coefficients are small. So the place to look is the fine-scale wavelet marginals near zero.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Needs:** section 6's first cell (it defines `sample_path` and `needs_norm`). Run that cell first if you haven't.\n",
    "\n",
    "**What it shows (data `x1` vs the final samples of each seed):**\n",
    "1. **The 11 statistics on the final samples:** (model − data)/data. Negative = the model has too little in that region.\n",
    "2. **Per channel, for both Scalar banks:**\n",
    "   - the KS distance between the data and model coefficient marginals, next to a **noise floor**: the KS between two halves of the data, i.e. what sampling noise alone gives;\n",
    "   - the share of coefficients in the **core** (|z| below the first region cut) and in region 1, data vs model.\n",
    "3. **A bar plot of KS per channel**, with the channels that carry a missed statistic in red.\n",
    "4. **Histograms of |coefficient| on log-log axes**, which zoom on the core, for the missed channels and a few control channels. Dashed lines = region cuts.\n",
    "\n",
    "**How to read it.**\n",
    "- KS far above the floor **only on the red channels**, and too little core share on the model → the 11 misses *are* the fine-scale marginal problem you see. Then decide whether the paper needs fine-scale sparsity right.\n",
    "- Red channels about as good as the controls → the misses barely change the marginal you look at, and the iterated corrector is not worth it for this.\n",
    "- Other channels bad too → the marginal problem has another cause as well.\n",
    "\n",
    "Caveat: the shares use hard cuts on the raw |z|. The potential itself uses smooth windows and |z|^α weights, so shares and the statistics in table 1 need not move by the same amount."
